WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.350
Gone too soon, but not forgotten.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:08.220
These beloved actors may have tragically passed
away, but their famous faces will light up

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.920
the screen one more time in 2024.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:17.320
2023 has seen some particularly stunning losses
in show business, from "Friends" star Matthew

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:24.220
Perry, to "Brooklyn Nine-Nine" favorite Andre
Braugher to Albus Dumbledore himself, Michael Gambon.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.800
But the most shocking loss may be that of
promising young actor Angus Cloud.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.840
"At one point, I turned around and they had
the guns pointed at me, I'm like 'oh, smokes.'"

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:41.860
Known for his work on the hit HBO series "Euphoria,"
Cloud passed away unexpectedly at the age of 25.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:46.770
The actor, who played Fezco, a drug dealer
with a heart of gold, was declared dead after

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.870
being found in his California home.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.580
It was later revealed that the actor had suffered
an overdose of narcotics.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:58.090
Immediately, wishes of love and grief poured
in from Hollywood and Cloud's co-stars, especially

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:01.870
the young cast who worked alongside the performer
on "Euphoria."

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.360
Before his death, Cloud's star was on the
rise — and as a result, he signed on to

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.360
multiple projects that will now feature posthumous
performances.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:15.660
He already appeared in the 2023 thriller "Your
Lucky Day," which received a theatrical release

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:19.555
in November, and he's got two things in the
works for 2024.

00:01:19.555 --> 00:01:24.340
Fans of the late actor will be able to catch
him in the horror flick "Freaky Tales" alongside

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:30.470
Pedro Pascal and Ben Mendelsohn, as well as
an untitled Universal Monsters movie featuring

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:34.913
Melissa Barrera and Giancarlo Esposito.

00:01:34.913 --> 00:01:40.210
Fans of Ray Stevenson likely remember his
recent turn in the hit Star Wars series "Ahsoka,"

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:42.739
making the news of his passing all the more
tragic.

00:01:42.739 --> 00:01:49.369
Stevenson was an accomplished actor who starred
on huge shows like "Dexter," "Rome," and "Black

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:54.860
Sails," appeared in the Marvel Cinematic Universe
as Volstagg in the first three Thor films,

00:01:54.860 --> 00:02:01.260
and popped up in 2022's universally beloved
Telugu film "RRR," in which he portrays a

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.409
brutal British imperialist.

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:08.910
Sadly, Stevenson passed away in May of this
year while working on a project in Ischia,

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.119
an Italian island.

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:11.553
He was 58 years old.

00:02:11.553 --> 00:02:16.550
Technically, Stevenson's first posthumous
performance came in "Ahsoka," which pays tribute

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:21.620
to the late actor, but he still has one project
upcoming in 2024.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:27.680
Stevenson replaced disgraced actor Kevin Spacey
in the Hungarian action film "1242: Gateway

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.232
to the West," a drama about a priest managing
to stop an invasion by Mongols.

00:02:32.232 --> 00:02:36.780
When it is released, it will mark Stevenson's
final performance.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:41.260
Film and television fans are definitely familiar
with Lance Reddick, who was one of the best

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.780
parts of about a million different projects.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.680
"We implemented Casual Friday, where employees
can wear jeans, once a month!"

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.470
"Well that was a catastrophic mistake."

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:56.940
Whether people know him from "Oz," "Lost,"
"The Wire," "Fringe," or even the cult comedy

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:01.519
favorite "Corporate," Reddick was an incredible
character actor with an enormous number of

00:03:01.519 --> 00:03:02.909
credits to his name.

00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:08.774
Sadly, Reddick passed away from heart disease
on March 17 at the age of 60 at his California home.

00:03:08.774 --> 00:03:13.790
Co-stars paid tribute to Reddick's memory,
including his "John Wick" co-stars Ian McShane

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.250
and Keanu Reeves.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:23.730
"Lance is a… was, is… a very beautiful
person, a special artist."

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:28.069
It's appropriate that "John Wick: Chapter
4" was one of Reddick's first posthumous roles,

00:03:28.069 --> 00:03:32.705
as a spin-off movie set in the same universe
will also feature a performance from him.

00:03:32.705 --> 00:03:38.090
Some of Reddick's other posthumous releases
in 2023 included the remake of "White Men

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:44.210
Can't Jump," "The Caine Mutiny Court-Martial,"
"Bosch: Legacy," and "Percy Jackson and the Olympians."

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:49.099
Audiences can see his final turn as Charon
, the concierge of the New York City Continental

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:54.500
Hotel when the John Wick spin-off film "Ballerina"
hits theaters in 2024.

